      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Oh interesting, this sound like a privacy versus accessibility issue. How much information could the platform identification of the world reveal versus the benefits of revealing hidden information for accessibility? I know it is fairly negligible in most situations but it is still revealing what should essentially be private information. \n\nIt should indeed alert users if it is a supported world considering it does anyway after receiving the confirmation request, unless it is hidden behind that confirmation request because it is private information.  \n\nJust remember, if this information is revealed, to apply this to all clients as PC users would need to know if it is a Quest only world too.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
